      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "So they sought for a beautiful young lady throughout all the borders of Israel, and found Abishag the Shunammite, and brought her to the king."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Bathsheba went in to the king in his room. The king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite was serving the king."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "He said, “Please speak to Solomon the king (for he will not tell you ‘no’), that he give me Abishag the Shunammite as wife.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "She said, “Let Abishag the Shunammite be given to Adonijah your brother as wife.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 2:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "King Solomon answered his mother, “Why do you ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? Ask for him the kingdom also, for he is my elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.”"
      }
